<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n10944" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">contus</span></b> , i, m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κοντός</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a pole, pike</i> (perh. not ante-Aug.), as an
			implement of a boat or ship, <i><span class="en">Verg. A. 5,
				208</span></i>; <i><span class="en">6, 302</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Tac. A. 14,
			5</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Suet. Calig. 32</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">as a weapon,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Verg.
					A. 9, 510</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Tac. A. 6, 35</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. H. 1,
			44</span></i>.—Prov.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">non contis et remulco ferri, ut aiunt, sed
					velificatione plenā,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Amm. 18, 5, 6</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pedalis, i. q. membrum virile,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Auct. Priap. 10, 3</span></i>
			.</div>
